|  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n\nthat we can rewrite as:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we orthogonalize ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process to get the corresponding orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nLet ${c}_{1}={b}_{1},$ then:\n\n|  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${c}_{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-7}} |  |  |\n\nFinally, normalizing orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-8}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-9}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-10}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-11}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Factor in the SVD of a Rectangular Matrix: Cases Requiring Orthogonalization" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048143 :topic/math-academy-id 3133 :topic/title "Singular Value Decomposition of Larger Matrices"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162046 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f_{Y}(y) = {8e^{-8y},\\begin{vmatrix}y > 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158691} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f_{Y}(y) = {2e^{-2y},\\begin{vmatrix}y > 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158692} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{1}{2}e^{-4y},\\begin{vmatrix}y > 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158693} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f_{Y}(y) = {2e^{-4y},\\begin{vmatrix}y > 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158694} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{1}{4}e^{-4y},\\begin{vmatrix}y > 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158695}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158690}] :question/math-academy-id "q-108501" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n$f_{X}(x) = {4e^{-4x},\\begin{vmatrix}x > 0 \\